I expect the kernel `conformance.kernel.recovered-from-prose` to move when the transform `conformance.transform.prose-before` is applied to a bare JSON object. According to the registry, this kernel determines "Whether the harness had to recover the object from prose or a fence (yes) or read it as strict JSON (no)". A bare JSON object is read as strict JSON (no), but adding the sentence 'Here is the form:' before it via `conformance.transform.prose-before` makes the reply no longer strict JSON, forcing the harness to recover the object from prose (yes).